@name Canon EF 24-70mm f/2.8L II - US 8,736,971 ex. 3
# Canon patent US 8,736,971 B2, numerical example 3 (https://patents.google.com/patent/US8736971B2/en).
# Bill Claff's Optical Bench Hub lists this example as the EF 24-70mm f/2.8L II USM; it has that
# lens' 18 elements in 13 groups (one Super UD, two UD, three aspherical elements).
# Radii, spacings, nd/vd and aspheric coefficients are the patent's. Assumed (see the .md file):
# - patent surface 16 (flat, 1.90 mm before the stop) dropped, its 1.90 mm added to d15; the stop
#   sits 0.01 mm before surface 18 (patent: 0.00);
# - semi-diameters: unvignetted f/2.91 axial and corner bundles over the zoom range, +0.3 mm,
#   cut where neighbouring surfaces meet;
# - Canon specifies 9 rounded blades; the blade curvature is a guess.
@iris 9 0.8
@coating multi
# Patent focal lengths (wide, middle, tele), the variable gaps d5, d15, d24, d33 (back focus) and
# the F-number at each (the stop opening follows it).
@zoom 24.70 34.93 67.88
@zoom-gap 5 2.75 11.72 30.30
@zoom-gap 15 15.65 9.62 2.12
@zoom-gap 23 8.79 4.80 0.74
@zoom-gap 32 38.08 46.62 63.32
@zoom-fnumber 2.91 2.91 2.91
